From a34c12849afe6d7ccd0d425b6e098b0c9f876753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verity sp1-tcdot lane <lane@verity.local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:44:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add TC_DOT_BF16: BF16 operands through the shared TC_DOT
 GroupSum back end

Ampere mma.sync m16n8k16 bf16 semantics (groups [8, 8], width 25, floor -132,
truncation) for one accumulator coordinate per row. The fp8 TC_DOT chip's
operand-independent back end (C term, GroupSum stages, G1 term, fp32 pack) is
factored into shared helpers parameterised by TcPipeline; the fp8 constraints
are unchanged. New: syscall 0x00_01_01_37, RiscvAirId TcDotBf16/TcDotBf16User,
reference kernel try_tc_dot_bf16_witness (non-panicking contract check),
guest stub syscall_tc_dot_bf16, prove + negative-soundness tests.
